What:		/sys/bus/wmi/devices/0B30FD67-1B62-4FCA-B10B-50DC7ADE6A39-*/copilot_mode_raw
What:		/sys/bus/wmi/devices/0B30FD67-1B62-4FCA-B10B-50DC7ADE6A39-*/keyboard_backlight_raw
What:		/sys/bus/wmi/devices/0B30FD67-1B62-4FCA-B10B-50DC7ADE6A39-*/battery_mode_raw
What:		/sys/bus/wmi/devices/0B30FD67-1B62-4FCA-B10B-50DC7ADE6A39-*/battery_ec_raw
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	linux-acpi@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RO, 0400) Raw diagnostic attributes for unmapped or
		unverified firmware state. Intentionally restricted to root
		read-only; candidates for relocation to debugfs prior to
		upstream drivers/platform/x86 inclusion:
		- copilot_mode_raw: raw EC mailbox byte (0 or 4) from GCLS (0x03/0x05).
		- keyboard_backlight_raw: two space-separated hex bytes from
		  GKBT (0x03/0x0B) ("<mailbox_reg> <mailbox_ext_reg>").
		- battery_mode_raw: raw byte (0, 1, or 2) from GBMM (0x03/0x0D).
		- battery_ec_raw: two sequential non-atomic 15-byte hex dumps
		  ("first=<30hex> second=<30hex>") of board-specific H_EC
		  registers 0x84..0x89, 0x8C..0x93, 0xA8.

What:		/sys/bus/wmi/devices/0B30FD67-1B62-4FCA-B10B-50DC7ADE6DDD-*/event_state
What:		/sys/bus/wmi/devices/0B30FD67-1B62-4FCA-B10B-50DC7ADE6DDD-*/event_log
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	linux-acpi@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RO, 0400) Diagnostic WMI notification counters and ring buffer
		for _WED(0xD0) events ("count=<n> last=0x<code8>" and up to 32
		lines of "<seq> <boottime_ns> 0x<code8>"). Intended for hotkey
		validation and candidate for debugfs before upstream submission.

What:		/sys/bus/wmi/devices/C75665A3-4382-4646-ADC8-C81AE146E455-*/auto_power_on
Date:		November 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	linux-acpi@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RO/RW) AC power-on recovery setting ("0" or "1"), backed by
		board EC register 0xF5 (0x00=off, 0xa0=on). Default mode is
		0444; becomes 0644 when loaded with allow_autopower_writes=1,
		writing through standard WMI method WMCC followed by settling
		delay and EC readback verification.
